WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue {
    color: white;
    background-color: #383943A3;
}

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.440
Maya stayed in – but because Javi insisted, not because
she understood why.

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:06.846
That distinction matters.

00:00:06.846 --> 00:00:12.384
The next time she's in a similar situation – before
a big presentation, before a difficult meeting, before

00:00:12.384 --> 00:00:16.714
any moment that needs her at her best – Javi won't
be there to override her.

00:00:17.914 --> 00:00:20.595
She needs the reasoning, not just the outcome.

00:00:20.596 --> 00:00:26.110
The reasoning is straightforward: orientation is where
you learn how the place actually works.

00:00:26.110 --> 00:00:29.884
Who does what, what the expectations are, what the
first weeks involve.

00:00:29.884 --> 00:00:32.171
You can't get that from the job description.

00:00:33.371 --> 00:00:36.841
Walking in tired means you're taking in about half
of it.

00:00:36.841 --> 00:00:41.533
The information pack on the table would help with
the rest – it's what companies send so you arrive

00:00:41.533 --> 00:00:42.671
with some context.

00:00:42.671 --> 00:00:43.959
It's still unopened.